    "notes": {
        "ba30b697-4b51-4ee3-976d-359b9d0544a3": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 304,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\nThe queue **appmixer-e2e-send-to-queue** must exist on the broker of the connected account: the components never declare queues. Create it in the RabbitMQ management UI (Queues → Add queue, durable).\n\nThe message is sent with `expiration` 120000 ms, so a message left over from a failed run is gone before the next run. Don't run this flow twice within two minutes. Keep only one consumer on this queue: a second consumer takes the message away from this flow."
        }
